In article <25598@cs.yale.edu> beigel-richard@CS.YALE.EDU (Richard Beigel) writes:

>I think that weapon restrictions are not currently enforced, but they
>should be.  I think that it upsets game balance when priests, dwarves,
>and wizards can use a longswords (no edged weapons classically allowed
>for priests, dwarves are too short, and wizards can't use anything
>bigger than a dagger), and lawful characters can use Stormbringer.

I don't agree that weapon restrictions should be enforced. Every fantasy
game doesn't have to follow AD&D rules. Why do you say that wizards
can't use anything bigger than a dagger? Gandalf in the Tolkien books
used a sword. If a wizard or a priest in NetHack should come across a
sword, they should be able to use it like anyone else with similar
statistics. The reason knights and such can use swords better is their
better strength and dexterity than the average wizard.

